<section class="safari-more-details">
    <div class="container">
        <h3>River Canoeing in Amaltari</h3>
        <p>
            Glide along the tranquil waters of the Narayani River and explore the rich aquatic and riverside wildlife of Chitwan National Park. This peaceful canoeing experience offers a unique opportunity to see animals up close from the water level, making it ideal for bird watchers and wildlife photographers.
        </p>

        <h3>Canoeing Schedule</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Morning Shift:</strong> 6:30 AM – 8:00 AM</li>
            <li><strong>Evening Shift:</strong> 4:00 PM – 5:30 PM</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Early mornings and late afternoons are the best times for bird watching and spotting animals along the riverbanks.
        </p>

        <h3>Pickup and Drop-off</h3>
        <p>
            We offer <strong>pickup and drop-off</strong> from your hotel or community lodge around Amaltari. Canoeing begins from designated river entry points, and guests are transported back comfortably after the ride.
        </p>

        <h3>Route and Highlights</h3>
        <p>
            The canoe ride generally follows a calm stretch of the Narayani or Rapti rivers depending on water levels. Key highlights include:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Rapti River Shoreline:</strong> Frequent sightings of crocodiles and bird flocks.</li>
            <li><strong>Narayani Sandbanks:</strong> Ideal location for spotting marsh muggers and gharials.</li>
            <li><strong>Jungle river corridor:</strong> Monitor lizards, otters, and migratory birds along the edges.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What to Expect</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Close encounters with <strong>gharial crocodiles</strong>, <strong>marsh muggers</strong>, and <strong>turtles</strong>.</li>
            <li>Sightings of <strong>over 100 bird species</strong> including storks, herons, kingfishers, and Brahminy kites.</li>
            <li>A quiet and scenic experience, perfect for <strong>nature lovers</strong> and <strong>photographers</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Guidelines to Follow</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Do not stand or move abruptly inside the canoe.</li>
            <li>Wear the life jacket provided at all times.</li>
            <li>Do not attempt to touch or feed any wildlife.</li>
            <li>Keep noise to a minimum to avoid disturbing animals.</li>
            <li>Photography is encouraged, but no flash near animals.</li>
        </ul>

        <p><em>Note: Canoeing is weather and water-level dependent. Activities may be postponed or rerouted for safety.</em></p>
    </div>
</section>



